ue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.8.dev1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nImproved `Tree` drag and drop #112993 was merged before Sticky `TreeItems` #115697, though the latter was implemented first, leading to unhandled behaviour when dragging over sticky parents.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aaeaa8a2-07ef-42d4-88ae-e185238cb985\n\nThere's two steps to fixing this, I think.\n\n1. The lines must recalculate themselves to be shorter, since their parent is visible sooner.\n2. The sticky parents should correctly report their [`get_item_at_position`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tree.html#class-tree-method-get-item-at-position) and [`get_drop_section_at_position`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tree.html#class-tree-method-get-drop-section-at-position).\n\nFeel free to make me an assignee.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake a SceneTree long enough to have sticky items appear, then try dragging onto parent.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","or